-- title:
--   Tame-1 inertia stabilises the transported Igusa discs, q=3
-- statement:
--   Numerical data. A prime $q$ with $q = 3$; a non-zero natural number $M'$ with $q \nmid M'$; a prime $\ell$ with $\ell \equiv 11 \pmod{12}$ and $\ell \mid M'$. A valuation subring $A$ of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}} =$ `AlgebraicClosure ℚ` with `hA : A.LiesOverPrime q`, i.e. $q$ lies in the non-units of $A$. An element $\pi \in \overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ with $\pi^{q^2-1} = q$ and $\pi \in A$.
--
--   Function fields. `modularFunctionFieldC (ResidueField A) M'` is the subfield of Laurent series over the residue field of $A$ generated by the $q$-expansions $j$ and $j(q^{M'})$; `modularFunctionFieldBar M'` is the subfield of `LaurentSeries (AlgebraicClosure ℚ)` obtained by adjoining to $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ the coefficientwise images of the full-level field `modularFunctionFieldFull M'`; and `fieldBar q M'` is the corresponding base change of `xHFunctionField (q ^ 2 * M') (levelH q M')`, where `levelH q M'` is the kernel of the reduction map $(\mathbb{Z}/q^2M')^\times \to (\mathbb{Z}/q)^\times$, that is the group of units congruent to $1$ modulo $q$. The hypothesis `hle` asserts the inclusion `modularFunctionFieldBar M' ≤ fieldBar q M'`.
--
--   Supersingular places and the constant reduction. $W$ is a finite set of places of `modularFunctionFieldC (ResidueField A) M'` over `ResidueField A` whose members are, by `hW`, exactly the supersingular places `ssPlaces q M' (ResidueField A)`: the rational affine geometric places at which the generic $j$-value lies in the supersingular set `ssJSet q`. $R_0$ is a `ConstantReduction` of $A$ from `modularFunctionFieldBar M'` to `modularFunctionFieldC (ResidueField A) M'` (a valuation subring of integers, a surjective residue map with kernel the maximal ideal, compatibility with $A$ and its residue map, a scaling clause, and a place map preserving degrees and orders). The hypothesis `hR₀` requires $R_0$ to be coefficientwise: for every Laurent series $y$ over $A$ whose image under `coeffMap A.subtype` lies in `modularFunctionFieldBar M'`, that image lies in `R₀.integers` and its $R_0$-residue, read as a Laurent series over `ResidueField A`, is the coefficientwise reduction of $y$.
--
--   Level automorphisms. $\zeta$ is an element of `Idx q`, a primitive $q$-th root of unity in $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$; `levelAutBar q M' ζ' γ` is the $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$-automorphism of `fieldBar q M'` characterised by the $q$-expansion identity `IsLevelAutBar` for $\zeta'$ and $\gamma$ (the identity if no such automorphism exists), and `redQ q γ` is the reduction of $\gamma$ modulo $q$ in $\mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb{Z}/q)$ acting on [`CuspidalType.ProjLine q`](def/CuspidalType_IsCuspidalOfType.html#L21).
--
--   The two families of valuation subrings. `OIg` assigns a valuation subring of `fieldBar q M'` to each point of [`CuspidalType.ProjLine q`](def/CuspidalType_IsCuspidalOfType.html#L21), and `OSS` assigns one to each member of $W$. The Igusa group of hypotheses: `hIg_inf` describes `OIg (lineInfty q)` as the set of $f$ for which there are Laurent series $x, y$ over $A$ with the coefficientwise reduction of $y$ non-zero and $f \cdot y = x$ coefficientwise over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$; `hIg` states that every point of the projective line is $\mathrm{red}_q(\gamma) \cdot \infty$ for some $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$ with `OIg` at that point the pullback of `OIg (lineInfty q)` along `levelAutBar q M' ζ γ` (the bound variable of `hIg` ranges over [`CuspidalType.ProjLine q`](def/CuspidalType_IsCuspidalOfType.html#L21), shadowing the prime $\ell$); `hIg_inj` states that `OIg` is injective; `hIg_perm` states that for every $\zeta'$ and every $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$ pulling back along `levelAutBar q M' ζ' γ` permutes the family `OIg`. The supersingular group: `hSS_A` says that for each $s \in W$ an element of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ lies in `OSS s` precisely when it lies in $A$; `hSS_over` says that for $s \in W$ and $f$ in `R₀.integers` having non-negative order at every place of `modularFunctionFieldBar M'` over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ at which the coefficientwise image of the $q$-expansion `jq` has non-negative order, if the $R_0$-residue of $f$ lies in the valuation subring of $s$ then the image of $f$ in `fieldBar q M'` lies in `OSS s`, and for every $a \in A$ whose residue equals the value of that $R_0$-residue at $s$ the difference $f - a$ lies in the maximal ideal of `OSS s`; `hSS_fix` says each `OSS s` is invariant under pullback along every `levelAutBar q M' ζ' γ` with $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$; `hSS_tr` provides for each $s$ an element $t \in$ `OSS s` such that $t - a$ is a unit of `OSS s` for every $a \in A$.
--
--   Charts at $\infty$ and the disc family. `Cinf` and the family `CIg` indexed by [`CuspidalType.ProjLine q`](def/CuspidalType_IsCuspidalOfType.html#L21) are `ComponentChart`s for $A$ from `fieldBar q M'` to `xHFunctionFieldC (ResidueField A) (q ^ 2 * M') (levelH q M')`, and `RI` is a `RegularProlongation` between the same fields with `RI.integers = OIg (lineInfty q)`; `hCinfint` and `hCinfres` say that `Cinf` has the same ring of integers as `RI` and the same residue map on it. `NIg` is a finite set of places of the target field, `discI` assigns to each such place a set of places of `fieldBar q M'` over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ and `coordI` a coordinate in `fieldBar q M'`; `hnodesI` identifies `Cinf.nodes` with `NIg`, and `hfamI` asserts `RI.DiscFamily NIg discI coordI`: for $Q \notin$ `NIg` the set `discI Q` is a residue disc for `RI` with coordinate `coordI Q`, and discs attached to distinct places off `NIg` are disjoint. `SI` assigns a subring of `fieldBar q M'` to each place of the target field and `χ₀I Q` a ring homomorphism from `SI Q` to `ResidueField A`. The stalk hypothesis `hstalkI` requires, for $Q \notin$ `NIg`, that every element of `SI Q` lie in `RI.integers` and that a place $P$ belong to `discI Q` exactly when $P$ is rational, every $f \in$ `SI Q` lies in the valuation subring of $P$ with $P$-value in $A$, and for every $f \in$ `SI Q` the $A$-valuation of that value is $< 1$ if and only if $\chi_{0I}(Q)(f) = 0$. The hypotheses `hdomI`, `hpmI` and `hpmI_off` say that `Cinf.dom` is the union of the discs `discI Q` over $Q \notin$ `NIg`, that `Cinf.placeMap` sends each place of `discI Q` to $Q$ for such $Q$, and that `Cinf.placeMap` is constant outside `Cinf.dom`.
--
--   Equivariance and transport. Let $G$ denote the subgroup of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$-automorphisms of `fieldBar q M'` generated by the automorphisms `levelAutBar q M' ζ' γ` with $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$. For $\tau \in G$ preserving `RI.integers`, `hNstabI` states that the induced residue automorphism `RI.resAut τ` preserves the set `NIg` of nodes, and `hdiscstabI` states that for $Q \notin$ `NIg` the transported disc `RegularProlongation.smulDisc τ (discI Q)` $= \{P \mid \tau^{-1} \cdot P \in$ `discI Q`$\}$ equals `discI` at `RI.resAut τ • Q`. The map $g$ assigns to each point of [`CuspidalType.ProjLine q`](def/CuspidalType_IsCuspidalOfType.html#L21) an automorphism in $G$, with `hg` providing $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$ such that $\mathrm{red}_q(\gamma) \cdot \infty$ is that point and $g$ at it equals `levelAutBar q M' ζ γ`, and `hCIg_def` defines `CIg ℓ` as the pullback `Cinf.comap (g ℓ)`.
--
--   Inertia hypotheses. Writing $\rho$ for the semilinear action [`ModularCurve.arithmeticGalois (xHFunctionField (q ^ 2 * M') (levelH q M'))`](def/ModularCurve_ArithmeticGalois.html#L54), which makes an automorphism $\tau$ of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ over $\mathbb{Q}$ act coefficientwise on `fieldBar q M'` and on its places: `hSI_inert` states that for $\tau$ in the inertia subgroup `A.inertiaSubgroupIn ℚ` with `A.tameCharacter π τ = 1` and for $Q \notin$ `NIg`, an element of `fieldBar q M'` lies in `SI Q` if and only if its image under $\rho(\tau)$ does; `hχ₀I_inert` states that $\chi_{0I}(Q)$ is unchanged by this action on `SI Q`.
--
--   Conclusion. For every $\tau$ in `A.inertiaSubgroupIn ℚ` with `A.tameCharacter π τ = 1`, for every point $\ell$ of [`CuspidalType.ProjLine q`](def/CuspidalType_IsCuspidalOfType.html#L21) (again shadowing the prime $\ell$), every place $Q$ of `xHFunctionFieldC (ResidueField A) (q ^ 2 * M') (levelH q M')` with $Q \notin$ `NIg`, and every place $P$ of `fieldBar q M'` over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$: $P$ lies in the transported disc $\{P \mid g(\ell) \cdot P \in$ `discI Q`$\}$ if and only if $\rho(\tau) \cdot P$ lies in that same set.
--
--   This is a step in the assembly of the semistable covering of the modular curve of level $q^2M'$ with $H$ the units congruent to $1$ modulo $q$, in the case $q = 3$, where the rigidifying condition that $M'$ be divisible by a prime $\ell \equiv 11 \pmod{12}$ is imposed: it records that the discs of the chart at $\infty$, transported along the level automorphisms $g(\ell)$ to the Igusa components, are stable under the coefficientwise action of the inertia elements of tame character $1$. It is used by [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.exists_semistableCovering_equivClauses_of_valuationSubrings_semistableModel_inertiaInfty_charted_of_eq_three_of_dvd`](thm.html#ModularCurve.FullLevel.exists_semistableCovering_equivClauses_of_valuationSubrings_semistableModel_inertiaInfty_charted_of_eq_three_of_dvd), and rests on the description of the discs as section sets of the stalks `SI Q` cut out by the characters `χ₀I Q` together with the commutation of tame-character-$1$ inertia with the level automorphisms.
